Done. One file changed and committed.

## What I changed

Only `.context/check-nav-coverage.mjs`. The checker now:

1. **Expands dynamic segments generically** ΓÇö for any `[param]` page (not just `locations`), it reads the page source, resolves each project-relative import (`@/ΓÇª`, `./ΓÇª`, `../ΓÇª`) to a real file with extension probing, and extracts slug literals via `slug\s*:\s*['"`]([^'"`]+)['"`]/g`. Each slug becomes a concrete route. This resolves both `/locations/fractional-cto/[location]` and `/locations/tech-audit/[location]` from `data/locations.ts` (27 slugs each ΓåÆ 54 dynamic pages).
2. **Leaves ORPHANED detection unchanged** ΓÇö it still runs on static literal directory names only, so the 14 orphans are untouched.
3. **Adds an `UNRESOLVED DYNAMIC` advisory section** ΓÇö segments that can't be enumerated (e.g. `/blog/[slug]`, which is hub-authoritative) are listed, and any nav link matching their pattern is treated as satisfied, never broken.

No TS execution, no new dependencies ΓÇö still plain node ESM with `fs`/`path` only. Nav files, `data/locations.ts`, and package files untouched.

